-- ===================== Other =====================

-- netFORUM Enterprise: correct the auth declaration, and pin the declared catalog's freshness.
--
-- TWO DEFECTS, one root cause — a declaration that no longer describes the thing it declares.
--
-- 1. THE AUTH PROSE WAS WRONG (CredentialType.Description, CredentialType.FieldSchema,
--    Integration.Configuration.AuthFlowNote / AuthHeaderPattern / AuthHeaderPatternNote /
--    TransportMode / TransportModeNote).
--
--    Every one of those said the connector POSTs to <BaseURL>/xWeb/JSON/Authenticate with HTTP
--    Basic auth and receives an "Authorization: Bearer <token>" for later calls. It does not, and
--    has not on this code path. NetForumConnector.Authenticate() POSTs a SOAP envelope:
--
--        POST <BaseURL>/xweb/secure/netForumXML.asmx
--        Content-Type: text/xml; charset=utf-8
--        SOAPAction: http://www.avectra.com/2005/Authenticate
--        <soap:Body><Authenticate xmlns="http://www.avectra.com/2005/">
--          <userName>…</userName><password>…</password>
--        </Authenticate></soap:Body>
--
--    The credentials are BODY ELEMENTS — no HTTP Authorization header is set on this call at all —
--    and the token is the string in <AuthenticateResult>. Every later call carries it as a SOAP
--    HEADER ELEMENT built by BuildSoapEnvelope():
--
--        <soap:Header><AuthorizationToken xmlns="http://www.avectra.com/2005/">
--          <Token>{token}</Token></AuthorizationToken></soap:Header>
--
--    The connector's own file header has said so verbatim the whole time — "Auth (TWO-STEP, SOAP —
--    NOT HTTP Basic / WWW-Authenticate / Bearer)" — so the metadata contradicted the code it cited.
--    It cited it as "NetForumConnector.ts:326-357", a line range that now lands on unrelated code:
--    a line-number citation rots silently. The replacement prose cites SYMBOLS (Authenticate(),
--    BuildSoapEnvelope(), SoapHeaders()), which survive edits.
--
--    Why this is worth a migration rather than a doc fix: CredentialType.Description and
--    FieldSchema are what an operator READS while filling in the credential form, and they are
--    served from the tenant catalog — not from this repo. An operator debugging a failed
--    connection was being told to look for a Bearer header that never exists on the wire.
--    TransportMode also changes soap_with_json_shim -> soap: the JSON shim is not called by this
--    connector and its existence is unverified from this repo, so the declared value now states
--    what the code does rather than an unexercised alternative.
--
-- 2. THE DECLARED CATALOG HAD NO FRESHNESS RECORD (new Integration.Configuration.DeclaredAgainst).
--
--    The catalog is derived from the vendor's public xWeb WSDL. The only provenance carried was
--    three keys buried inside WSDLOperationCounts (primaryWSDLSource, crossVerifiedSource,
--    accessedAt), which is a COUNTS object — the fetch date read as a footnote to a statistic
--    rather than as the catalog's evidence base. Those three keys move into a DeclaredAgainst
--    block (the convention already used by LMS/Elevate and Platform/WordPress), and the block
--    additionally records what is NOT pinned, because an unrecorded gap reads as a settled fact:
--
--      * sha256 of the 5.94 MB WSDL — never captured, so a refetch cannot be diffed against what
--        was actually declared from. totalUniqueOperations (277) is the only comparable and a bare
--        count can collide (one op removed, another added, nets to zero).
--      * docSitesFetchedAt — the Abila 2017.1 pages are cited throughout the Configuration
--        (GetQuery @TOP semantics, DataGrid row-limit behaviour) but were never date-stamped.
--      * tenantReleaseVersion — the two source WSDLs are LIVE tenant instances of unknown release,
--        read against a 2017.1 doc set. With no version pinned, a later "missing" object cannot be
--        attributed: catalog wrong, or tenant older? Platform/WordPress pins wp 7.1 /
--        woocommerce 11.0.1 with zip sha256s for exactly this reason.
--      * catalogLastEditedAt — "source fetched" and "catalog edited" are different dates.
--        V202607280915 (WritablePK) edited the catalog on 2026-07-27, 37 days after the pin. That
--        edit was reasoned from the same 2026-06-20 WSDL read, so the pin still describes the
--        evidence base — but nothing recorded that, so a reader could not tell whether a post-pin
--        edit was evidence-backed or freehand. Now they can.
--
--    This is unrelated to the repo-wide A9 check (scripts/check-catalog-freshness.mjs), which
--    compares package version to git tag and says nothing about the vendor surface.
--
-- No object rows, no field rows, no IDs and no capability flags change. Reads and writes are
-- byte-for-byte unaffected; this migration moves only declared text.
--
-- DELTA migration, deliberately not a re-seed: the rows already exist on installed tenants, so the
-- V202606271422 seed stays untouched and applied — no UUID re-minted, no Flyway checksum broken.
-- Both statements are idempotent (keyed by the seeded row ID).

-- ── 1. Integration.Configuration — corrected auth keys + new DeclaredAgainst block ──
